OL,3,GNEWSAMother with disabled son fears
OL,4,Arise in intolerance
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe mother of a boy with autism has
OL,7,Fsaid she is worried society is
OL,8,Fbeginning to feel less tolerant towards
OL,9,Fher son.
OL,11,FDarrell said her son Dexter, from
OL,12,FDevon, also has a speech impediment and
OL,13,Fthe mindset of a much younger child -
OL,14,Fbut his disabilities are not
OL,15,Fimmediately obvious.
OL,17,FShe said her son was "the most lovely
OL,18,Flad in the world" but he experienced
OL,19,Funpleasant encounters in public.
OL,23,APub: 09-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
